# Weekly Bible study session — shared fallback for any householder without a
# study_timeline of their own. Narration only (no portrait), so it works at
# any door. Outcomes: STUDY_CONTINUES keeps the study on the map as an
# appointment; REFUSED ends it.
# The study aid is "the study book" — generic on purpose; the real org's
# study books have titles, and naming one would be lifting.

You sit across from them at the kitchen table, the study book open between you.
You read the paragraph aloud, then the question printed beneath it. They answer in their own words, and you guide the answer back toward the paragraph.
if DoubtMeter.value >= 40:
	[signal arg="INNER_VOICE"]
	[i]They ask something the paragraph doesn't cover. You hear yourself give the answer you were given.[/i]
The hour goes quickly. At the door they ask whether the same time next week still works.
- "Same time next week."
	[signal arg="STUDY_CONTINUES"]
	[end_timeline]
- "I don't think I can keep coming."
	[signal arg="REFUSED"]
	[end_timeline]
